    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_06665f58eb2835782fc77c9434e95e74db4a8ca180d3030fb97bbc112c0c08f4",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "The same prime-local representation controls both arithmetic identities: threshold splitting and telescoping convert coprime-axis sums into F-convolutions, and the F-to-C exchange lemma pairs symmetric terms so product corrections cancel against the central contribution. In the semi-diagonal case this yields one inserted-shift C factor; in the full two-swap case the four-set reformulation yields paired nine-term F tables and then the two inserted-shift target.",
