    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_5b9c197219b98cd39e061424fc738297cdbde08c895ea1263d97fb0718c7a3e2",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "The semi-diagonal one-swap calculation separates into a stable global transform skeleton and a prime-local arithmetic obligation. Suppressing q>1 and G exposes the Perron, Mellin, and functional-equation steps that fix the swapped zeta factors; restoring gcd, Möbius, Ramanujan, and G data leaves those steps in place and creates a residual Dirichlet-series factor, which the appendix converts to C/F power-series algebra and proves equals the recipe's required local correction.",
