    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_9c0d52bf938110f8eb609927267d380835ca176f990bfadaf6a44f869bb58856",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "Perron truncation and the Farey decomposition are complementary controls on off-diagonal depth: the factor involving X/T^{|U|} removes swap grades longer than the polynomial can expose, while in the surviving two-swap grade a common reduced ratio M/N converts one product discrepancy into two coupled additive shifts, whose two nonzero Mellin directions generate the two swapped singular directions.",
